A||||3||GT-maniac||Erratic idling||||1||
Z||000000||GT-maniac||05-08-2000||11:44 PM||||My 85 V6 GT seems to idle very erratically. Hovering around 1000 rpm and and moving up or down a few hundred rpm from there. When it's started cold it idles at about 1500 and then when it warms up it drops to about 1000. Is that normal ? Also when I come to a quick stop sometimes the car will die completely.<BR>Seems to be a new EGR valve on there so that's probably not the problem.||||reg||1
Z||000001||RobertVol||05-09-2000||12:42 AM||||Our little fieros are notorious for these funky idleing issues. anyway are you getting any codes? check engine light ?<P>Check..<BR>Egr anyway - may be new but put in wrong<BR>IAC<P>My idle was off little for awhile and Finally got the Check engine light..then got code 32 or 35 replaced the IAC Sensor. Fixed the problem. But alot of Fieros start with a little high idle but even out after warming up <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT-maniac||05-09-2000||05:37 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by RobertVol:<BR><B>Our little fieros are notorious for these funky idleing issues. anyway are you getting any codes? check engine light ?<P>Check..<BR>Egr anyway - may be new but put in wrong<BR>IAC<P>My idle was off little for awhile and Finally got the Check engine light..then got code 32 or 35 replaced the IAC Sensor. Fixed the problem. But alot of Fieros start with a little high idle but even out after warming up </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well my check engine light does like to come on whenever I'm climbing long hills. usually stays on then until I restart the car. I'm waiting for my local Wal-mart to get a code reader in and then hopefully I'll be able to better see what's wrong. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Phil||05-09-2000||06:21 PM||||You don't need a code reader. Save your money and use it to buy a Haynes manual ($14-16) and follow the directions. The manual will be much better investment. In a nut shell you put the computer into dianostic mode(with a paper clip) and the check engine light will flash the codes.||||reg||1
